error[ffi_incomplete_record]: `INANON` does not name `hi`, and `fixedbugs-156-bit-fields.h` says the struct has it — `hi` is a bit-field, which no field can bind, so a `record` over this struct leaves it out by being `partial`
  at tests/golden/unsupported/fixedbugs-156-bit-fields-inside-an-anonymous-struct.hero:9:12
    |
  9 |     record INANON  #~ ffi_incomplete_record
    |            ^^^^^^
  note: mark the `record` `partial`: it binds the fields it names, C keeps the bits of `hi`, and comparing it or using it as a map key is refused, as for every `partial` record

